{"title":"What should I ask Sheilagh Ogilvie?","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/912390194/0/marginalrevolution~What-should-I-ask-Sheilagh-Ogilvie.html","date":1738835257000,"content":"<p>She is a Canadian economic historian at Oxford, here is from her <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://sheilaghogilvie.com/\" target=\"_blank\">home page</a>:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p>I am an economic historian. I explore the lives of ordinary people in the past and try to explain how poor economies get richer and improve human well-being. I’m interested in how social institutions – the formal and informal constraints on economic activity – shaped economic development between the Middle Ages and the present day.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>And:</p>\r\n<blockquote><p>My current research focusses on serfdom, human capital, state capacity, and epidemic disease. Past projects analysed guilds, merchants, communities, the family, gender, consumption, finance, proto-industry, historical demography, childhood, and social capital. I have a particular interest in the economic and social history of Central and Eastern Europe.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheilagh_Ogilvie\" target=\"_blank\">her Wikipedia page</a>.  Her <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/European-Guilds-Economic-Analysis-Princeton/dp/0691217025/ref=sr_1_2?crid=ZSF344HDSXJ6&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.yeOXITkX20850pefHGoaq8MU8wTUOdsnCF4_dCN4CeslK5nVfbx4Dkq2aQlmzKS-SsEtYCIGAtzAq9UzBzom0CzlouWvCvaByd_riTawgr_L6vCs22byHIYCIvvGUvSNMbyrbFG5nZElNVj2bTqBdYMLi_-7ZBdu5YLhmZ9qAMaQlvOAOsr4uEfhEHaYy6Q9tZI7IIO_g1pZ3ATRJbgxzw.CpZIKG19hO_lGk1RAYtgov3WTI1TohWEDdlj2186Gaw&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=sheilagh+ogilvie&amp;qid=1738792022&amp;sprefix=sheilagh+ogilvie%2Caps%2C109&amp;sr=8-2\" target=\"_blank\">book on guilds</a> is well known, and her latest is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.amazon.com/Controlling-Contagion-Epidemics-Institutions-Princeton/dp/0691255563/ref=sr_1_1?crid=ZSF344HDSXJ6&amp;dib=eyJ2IjoiMSJ9.yeOXITkX20850pefHGoaq8MU8wTUOdsnCF4_dCN4CeslK5nVfbx4Dkq2aQlmzKS-SsEtYCIGAtzAq9UzBzom0CzlouWvCvaByd_riTawgr_L6vCs22byHIYCIvvGUvSNMbyrbFG5nZElNVj2bTqBdYMLi_-7ZBdu5YLhmZ9qAMaQlvOAOsr4uEfhEHaYy6Q9tZI7IIO_g1pZ3ATRJbgxzw.CpZIKG19hO_lGk1RAYtgov3WTI1TohWEDdlj2186Gaw&amp;dib_tag=se&amp;keywords=sheilagh+ogilvie&amp;qid=1738791986&amp;sprefix=sheilagh+ogilvie%2Caps%2C109&amp;sr=8-1\" target=\"_blank\">Controlling Contagion: Epidemics and Institutions from the Black Death to Covid</a>.  Here are <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://scholar.google.com/scholar?hl=en&amp;as_sdt=0%2C47&amp;q=sheilagh+ogilvie&amp;oq=sheilagh\" target=\"_blank\">her main research papers</a>.</p>\r\n<p>So what should I ask her?</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2025/02/what-should-i-ask-sheilagh-ogilvie.html\">What should I ask Sheilagh Ogilvie?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/912390194/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/912390194/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/912390194/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/912390194/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/19/912390194/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com